% F44-FPUT: DEFECT 44.  .PUT HAD NO LIMIT, SO F=, E= AND .<#> COULD WRITE
% PAST THE 40-BYTE OUTPUT CONVERSION AREA, OVER THE TIME_STRING DESCRIPTOR,
% AND SHOW_TIME (THE XLOAD DATE ERROR) THEN ENDED STOIC.  PATCHED, A FIELD
% OVER 40 GIVES "FLOATING POINT OUTPUT CONVERSION ERROR."
FLOAT< DECIMAL
() I_ABORT ABORT !
"|" MSG 1.5 40 2 F= "|" MSG CR
"|" MSG 1.5 41 2 F= "|" MSG CR
"|" MSG 1.5 60 2 F= "|" MSG CR
"|" MSG 1.5 40 2 E= "|" MSG CR
"|" MSG 1.5 44 2 E= "|" MSG CR
TIME_STRING @ @ = CR
0 1 SHOW_TIME CR
12345 = CR
